Yes. I found the Atlas trail in GitHub after searching the **commit history** rather than only the current code index. That changes my assessment: **Atlas already exists as the beginnings of exactly this entity/navigation layer; the new OpenAlex-for-Sanskrit vision should extend it rather than create another ontology.**

## 1. What Atlas actually is right now

The key initial commit is:

[http://github.com/prx0r/patala/commit/c0e40b97077ffd9176bca90684428cacda1bbcfe](http://github.com/prx0r/patala/commit/c0e40b97077ffd9176bca90684428cacda1bbcfe)

It introduced the **Śaiva Tantra Atlas** with:

```text
AtlasEntity
AtlasRelation

Traditions
Texts
People
Concepts

typed edges
confidence-weighted edges
```

At that point it had:

```text
7 traditions
6 texts
7 people
6 concepts
44 relations
```

Then:

[http://github.com/prx0r/patala/commit/1dc7f6872075c4632350e6072c37e87eb26b8935](http://github.com/prx0r/patala/commit/1dc7f6872075c4632350e6072c37e87eb26b8935)

