# 3. PANDiT — highest-priority strategic partner

[http://panditproject.org/](http://panditproject.org/)

[http://panditproject.org/about](http://panditproject.org/about)

PANDiT explicitly models **works, people, places, institutions, manuscripts and secondary literature** across premodern South Asia. ([Pandit Project][1])

### How we use it

**Do not ingest it as truth.**

Use it as an authority/crosswalk source:

```text
PATA-W-00194
    sameAs?       PANDiT work X

PATA-P-0012
    sameAs?       PANDiT person Y

PATA-MS-8291
    cataloguedAs  PANDiT manuscript Z
```

Atlas page:

```text
Abhinavagupta

Pāṭala ID       PATA-P-0012
PANDiT          [...]
Wikidata        Q...
VIAF            ...
```

### Important

I did **not** find a clearly documented public PANDiT API in the current search.

So don't quietly build production scraping around it.

Phase 1:

```text
link + reconcile
```

Phase 2:

```text
contact PANDiT
ask for export/API/cooperation
```

This is exactly the sort of project where a real partnership is better than treating them as a website to scrape.

