# 4. GRETIL — easiest large corpus import

Official archival/mirror repo:

[http://github.com/INDOLOGY/GRETIL-mirror](http://github.com/INDOLOGY/GRETIL-mirror)

GRETIL is now available in a stable Git-based snapshot, including Unicode files and substantial TEI material. ([GitHub][2])

### Use it for

```text
Work
   ↓
TextInstance
   ↓
GRETIL electronic text
```

NOT:

```text
GRETIL file = canonical work
```

For every file extract:

```text
title
author attribution
source edition
inputter
encoding
GRETIL path
hash
license/notes
```

Then run entity resolution against Atlas.

This could expand Atlas's `Text` layer enormously almost immediately.

