# 17. Three kinds of external integration

I would actually encode this distinction into Atlas itself.

### A. AUTHORITY

External service specializes in canonical identity.

```text
Crossref → DOI
DataCite → DOI/data
ORCID → living researcher
ROR → institution
```

Pāṭala generally accepts identifier resolution but keeps provenance.

### B. SOURCE

External project supplies scholarly/textual information.

```text
GRETIL
SARIT
Muktabodha
PANDiT
NGMCP
C-SALT
```

Never automatically equate their assertions with truth.

### C. SURROGATE

External service physically hosts the artifact.

```text
IIIF manifest
Internet Archive scan
institution repository
```

Pāṭala stores the identity/link/provenance rather than duplicating unnecessarily.

That should literally be in the adapter schema:

```typescript
type ExternalIntegrationRole =
  | "AUTHORITY"
  | "SOURCE"
  | "SURROGATE"
  | "DISCOVERY";
```

OpenAlex = mostly `DISCOVERY`.

